invariant: INV-13
file: tcp_nonblocking_frame.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: a tcp-nonblocking handshake failure writes its alert in the clear
  after this side has installed its write key, sealing only once the session
  is connected, where RFC 9846 section 6 protects an alert under the current
  write key. bin/tcp_nonblocking_loop_test requires every handshake failure
  after that key, the first one included, to emit CH_ALERT_RECORD_LEN bytes
  that open under the peer's read key.

--- old
    if (r->t.keys) {
        size_t sealed_len = 0;
--- new
    if (r->t.state == CH_ST_CONNECTED) {
        size_t sealed_len = 0;
